{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-bd.9:000019:note_appended:sase-bd.9.1:6ad1ec0598c5a7e8d5967ae5a040ab8e7c7df3917ee1c6940838938eaa03b4fe","timestamp":"2026-07-30T20:32:31Z","actor":"sase-bd.9.1","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"sase-bd.9.1","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Fixed the clippy::question_mark denial at crates/sase_core/src/bead/read.rs:232 by collapsing the match on read_legacy_jsonl_issues into the ? form. Swept the workspace rather than stopping at the first reported error, which surfaced a second denial hidden behind it (clippy stops at the first error per crate): a needless_borrow at crates/sase_core/tests/bead_read_parity.rs:594 passing &stream where stream was already a reference. Verified with the exact commands core CI runs: cargo fmt --all -- --check clean, cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings clean, cargo test --workspace fully green (all suites, 0 failures; PYO3_PYTHON and LD_LIBRARY_PATH pointed at a 3.12 interpreter for the local pyo3 build). Committed and pushed to sase-core master as 407965e 'fix(bead): satisfy clippy in the doctor reader'. Master CI run 30578914929 for that commit concluded success with both jobs green: 'cargo fmt + clippy + test' and 'maturin build + import smoke'. Core master is no longer red, so release-plz can cut a release; PR #63 'chore: release v0.15.0' remains open for the core-release phase."}}
{"schema_version":1,"event_id":"sase-bd.9:000020:note_appended:sase-bd.9.2:0b938667bdd490f9af5d562ea01a9614420173cdbb8df43b425065634f4a628b","timestamp":"2026-07-30T20:54:55Z","actor":"sase-bd.9.2","operation":"note_appended","issue_id":"sase-bd.9.2","payload":{"kind":"note_appended","entry":"Merged sase-core release PR #63 (chore: release v0.15.0) after master went green on 407965e. Verified before merging that the refreshed release branch contained all four target commits (160ff9e, 293ccb2, 81a82d5, 6468cb9) plus the clippy fix, that all PR checks passed (cargo fmt+clippy+test, maturin build+import smoke), and that the proposed bump was a breaking 0.14.2 -> 0.15.0. Post-merge: master CI run 30580458464 green, Release-plz run 30580460440 green through 'publish to PyPI', tag v0.15.0 -> 803ff81 (the merge commit). Confirmed publication from the index, not the repo: 'uv pip install --no-cache sase-core-rs==0.15.0' into a clean 3.12 venv succeeded, tools/check_sase_core_rs_bindings exited 0 ('exposes all 230 bindings required'), bead_doctor_report is present, and bead_show against the live beads sidecar returned sase-bd.3 instead of raising 'unknown variant note_appended'. Published version to carry into floor-bump: 0.15.0. No repo file changes in this phase."}}
